# Keep LF in the WORKING COPY, not just in the blob.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on this machine, so without these a checkout rewrites files to CRLF. Two things
# break when that happens:
#
#  - Shell scripts shipped to Sherlock become unreadable to bash -- `$'\r': command not found`, or a
#    silently mangled `set -euo pipefail`, which is a miserable failure to attribute from a SLURM log.
#  - Byte-level cross-platform comparison of sources stops working. `presets.source_digest` normalises
#    line endings precisely so a Windows and a Linux checkout of identical code agree, but the ad-hoc
#    `find | xargs cat | sha256sum` check used to verify a cluster deployment does not, and it
#    disagreed for exactly this reason on 2026-08-18.
#
# The blobs are already LF; this pins the checkout to match.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.sbatch  text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
